6	//! `start_migrated_postgres` runs against an ephemeral Postgres in Docker. In CI (`CI` env
7	//! set) a missing Docker daemon is a HARD FAILURE; on a Docker-less laptop the test skips
8	//! (returns `None`) with a note. Used by every integration test file that needs a real
9	//! database.
10	//!
11	//! `app`/`send` are shared by the HTTP integration suites (`http_tenancy.rs`,
12	//! `http_memberships.rs`); this file is compiled per test binary via `mod support;`, so
13	//! binaries that only need `start_migrated_postgres` (e.g. `roundtrip.rs`, `tenancy_*.rs`,
14	//! `grpc_tenancy.rs`) would otherwise warn on the unused HTTP helpers under
15	//! `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` — hence `#[allow(dead_code)]` on them.
